    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d456">

                <pb facs="0464" n="374" xml:id="pg374"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.48/680b</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Russian Ambassador</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Bakhmeteff</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-09-10"><hi rendition="#italic">September 10,
                        1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Ambassador</hi>: I am pleased to note
                    your willingness to transfer to the American Red Cross 150,000 pairs of shoes,
                    for the purpose of supplying the Czecho-Slovaks with footwear, and cordially
                    approve of this effort to relieve suffering and to aid in the common cause.</p>
                <p>Notification of your proposal has been sent to the American Red Cross, together
                    with a request that the Czecho-Slovaks be informed of the fact that these shoes
                    were furnished by the Russian Embassy in Washington.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
